AB  - DEMO / SYNTHETIC SOURCE. All studies, authors, observations, and results below are invented for an offline layout preview. The synthetic mapping workflow integrates seasonal spectral and canopy-height observations for tree-species discrimination. We ask whether seasonal spectral and canopy-height information improve tree-species discrimination. A random-forest classifier combined two-season hyperspectral imagery with lidar canopy-height features. The synthetic dataset contains 120 four-species plots; training and evaluation use spatially separate stands. The comparison covers one simulated site; transfer to other forests, sensors, and rare species remains untested. Simulated held-out macro-F1 was 0.82 for spectral-plus-height features and 0.74 for the single-season spectral baseline.
